# 8. RECURRING TRANSACTIONS AND SCHEDULER AUDIT

If Phase 8 is implemented, inspect the actual recurring transaction scheduler.

Verify:

- Daily, weekly, monthly, and yearly recurrence rules supported by the application.
- Month-end behavior.
- Start and end dates.
- Timezone handling.
- Paused schedules.
- Cancelled schedules.
- Completed schedules.
- Missed occurrences.
- Occurrence history.
- Retry behavior.
- Concurrent job execution.
- Scheduler authorization.

### Duplicate prevention

Verify that each scheduled occurrence can create no more than one financial transaction.

Use database uniqueness constraints and transactional or idempotent processing where supported.

Simulate repeated scheduler runs and concurrent processing attempts.

Ensure a failed operation can be retried safely.

Do not mark an occurrence successful before the transaction is durably saved.

### Financial integrity

- Generated transactions must use the existing transaction system.
- Scheduled estimates must remain separate from actual transactions.
- Recurring schedules must not appear as completed transactions before generation.
- Generated transactions must not be included twice in analytics or reports.
- Pausing or cancelling a schedule must not silently delete historical transactions.
- Finora must not claim that an external bill was paid simply because a transaction record was generated.

If the scheduler is not configured in the deployed environment, document the exact missing configuration.

Do not claim automatic processing is active unless it has been verified.

